Here is a simple Discord bot using **discord.js (v14)**:

### 1. Prerequisites
First, make sure you have [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) installed, initialize a new project, and install `discord.js`:

```bash
npm init -y
npm install discord.js
```

### 2. The Code (`index.js`)

```javascript
const { Client, GatewayIntentBits } = require('discord.js');

// Create a new client instance
const client = new Client({
  intents: [
    GatewayIntentBits.Guilds,
    GatewayIntentBits.GuildMessages,
    GatewayIntentBits.MessageContent, // Required to read message text
  ],
});

// Run once when the bot is online
client.once('ready', () => {
  console.log(`Ready! Logged in as ${client.user.tag}`);
});

// Listen for incoming messages
client.on('messageCreate', (message) => {
  // Ignore messages sent by bots to avoid infinite loops
  if (message.author.bot) return;

  // Check if the message is "ping" (case-insensitive)
  if (message.content.toLowerCase() === 'ping') {
    message.reply('pong');
  }
});

// Log in to Discord using your bot token
// Replace 'YOUR_BOT_TOKEN_HERE' with your actual bot token from the Discord Developer Portal
client.login('YOUR_BOT_TOKEN_HERE');
```

### 3. Important Setup Note
For this to work, make sure to enable the **Message Content Intent** in your [Discord Developer Portal](https://discord.com/developers/applications):
1. Go to your bot's application page.
2. Click on the **Bot** tab on the left.
3. Scroll down to **Privileged Gateway Intents**.
4. Toggle **Message Content Intent** to **ON** and save changes.

Run your bot with:
```bash
node index.js
```

